<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 88,115 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 88,115 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 88,115 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 70,369 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	March 13</p>
<p>    Export cargo		26,746	19,903</p>
<p>    Import cargo		61,369	50,466</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, six are expected to sail and 11 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Courage    15/3</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-I	    15/3</p>
<p>Vehicles		    107	 Arcadia Highway    16/3</p>
<p>Containers		  240	 Dammam Bay	   19/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
